Create a command-line greeting program.

Include "greetings.nut".

Accept zero or one positional argument: the person's name.
With no name, greet "world". With a name, use that name exactly as supplied.
Write the greeting followed by a newline to standard output and exit with status 0.

If more than one argument is supplied, write "Usage: greet [name]" followed
by a newline to standard error, write nothing to standard output, and exit with status 2.
